"type": "concept", "title": "Depth as a dramatic and spatial device"}], "description": "The gist is to control attention through sharpness and blur."}, {"id": "c352cd67-f9b0-402c-9050-72dc9979777e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lens character and testing", "children": [{"id": "b6243624-50ac-40d7-a8dc-fcb93a3fdb1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Sharpness, contrast, flare, breathing, color, and aberration"}, {"id": "7b2a1e50-30a7-4bd4-a8ff-d7077b283cd4", "type": "concept", "title": "Prime versus zoom workflow"}, {"id": "1051622b-7dad-47f3-bcb1-8ba8108dc963", "type": "concept", "title": "Lens tests, charts, and subjective look evaluation"}], "description": "Students learn to evaluate lenses before relying on them."}]}, {"id": "bdf338f2-46fa-46d6-a15b-229b1777a01b", "type": "topic", "title": "Exposure, Dynamic Range, and the Digital Image", "description": "This topic teaches students how exposure decisions shape mood, texture, recoverability, and post-production flexibility.", "children": [{"id": "39d00b60-6e11-4c53-87d5-6eed196f530e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "The exposure triangle", "children": [{"id": "a6b1dd66-f8fc-4858-ba13-d43f1fc4757c", "type": "concept", "title": "ISO, EI, shutter angle, aperture, ND filtration"}, {"id": "056a07dc-5424-4cb7-989d-1c842d732648", "type": "concept", "title": "Motion blur, noise, and depth-of-field tradeoffs"}, {"id": "3f4f82fa-8dbe-4b7b-affc-bc2195c81208", "type": "concept", "title": "Manual exposure discipline"}], "description": "Students learn the practical relationship among aperture, shutter, and sensitivity."}, {"id": "393b50a0-3fb6-4069-a858-553ba1efe87a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dynamic range and latitude", "children": [{"id": "e294b6d8-fcc1-48f0-b627-3f5c6733af69", "type": "concept", "title": "Stops, clipping, noise floor, and middle gray"}, {"id": "535ad3c5-548f-49f0-bae4-60b1f96e5f36", "type": "concept", "title": "Log, raw, and baked image profiles"}, {"id": "80b519ab-81e0-49ca-8a4e-c5ad109a30e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Expose-to-the-right debates and production context"}], "description": "The point is to protect highlights, shadows, and skin tones."}, {"id": "c64e7079-9190-4b0f-a67a-8853c4d53011", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Measuring and controlling exposure", "children": [{"id": "25a8423a-60fc-409e-8160-0c91f996f495", "type": "concept", "title": "Incident and spot metering"}, {"id": "46268740-9bd6-43a6-a1f2-ad4cf2fd709d", "type": "concept", "title": "Waveform and false-color interpretation"}, {"id": "be9afdc3-1585-472a-babb-23bd2083c8ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Exposure consistency across coverage"}], "description": "Students connect meters and scopes to creative judgment."}]}, {"id": "157ccd75-bee7-416e-88ed-72d81628e71c", "type": "topic", "title": "Composition and Framing", "description": "Composition organizes attention inside the frame. This topic builds the visual literacy needed to make frames legible, expressive, and cinematic.", "children": [{"id": "feef199c-0d6a-4608-a779-dd5662bce0b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Frame geometry", "children": [{"id": "f515e4da-ab18-4cef-9317-8f194975718e", "type": "concept", "title": "Rule of thirds, symmetry, asymmetry, and center framing"}, {"id": "d6f61402-2670-46b4-9291-2fd3c71b7be6", "type": "concept", "title": "Leading lines, frames within frames, and layered depth"}, {"id": "0cc60ea3-ed48-4366-ac79-a4e32e5d3549", "type": "concept", "title": "Headroom, look room, eyelines, and screen direction"}], "description": "Students learn to compose through balance, line, shape, depth, and negative space."}, {"id": "ceaf8097-721e-42b3-b028-0e1b3a57aa72", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Aspect ratio and format", "children": [{"id": "e450662d-9fc5-4c1e-b6a5-8594f14960c4", "type": "concept", "title": "1.33, 1.66, 1.85, 2.39, vertical, square, and social formats"}, {"id": "5b8d0fca-2698-4673-8778-40d14d57e0f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Safe areas, reframing, and platform delivery"}, {"id": "c5d04337-34ec-4e80-bab4-88fc395e0801", "type": "concept", "title": "How aspect ratio changes blocking and staging"}], "description": "The goal is to design images for the chosen canvas."}, {"id": "2fc5c5ff-aacd-4a5d-9600-7ec702676952", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Composition for meaning", "children": [{"id": "fbcf07d4-9ff5-4b41-b100-68376ad718b3", "type": "concept", "title": "Power, isolation, intimacy, tension, and reveal"}, {"id": "4c65d808-45a9-4ef1-a2bd-e58f8a8afab2", "type": "concept", "title": "Subject-object relationships"}, {"id": "c3155f18-82b7-4c42-985b-348d6aac7725", "type": "concept", "title": "Foreground and background as story information"}], "description": "Students practice using framing as subtext."}]}, {"id": "b82ba40b-dac5-49ef-84f0-7d0c462192d6", "type": "topic", "title": "Camera Movement and Stabilization", "description": "Movement changes how viewers feel space and time. This topic teaches when to move, how to move, and when stillness is stronger.", "children": [{"id": "6026c5bb-f26f-4e96-81be-e428082e2a11", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Movement motivation", "children": [{"id": "0c89533d-3969-4beb-8ab9-8c2d6625e0d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Character movement, emotional shift, reveal, pursuit, and discovery"}, {"id": "5e3f507a-1758-44f8-a530-d9b4fd1dbc4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Stillness, drift, push, pull, pan, tilt, track, crane, and handheld"}, {"id": "eadfd15e-75a1-48ce-b60a-f602f4e0a219", "type": "concept", "title": "Rhythm and editorial consequences"}], "description": "Students learn to connect camera movement to story rather than decoration."}, {"id": "bac52198-65b2-49fb-84eb-17a51e8e3044", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tools and techniques", "children": [{"id": "dfc63f9c-f6a7-4c45-ad1e-99cb8d1a8ff7", "type": "concept", "title": "Tripod, dolly, slider, jib, crane, Steadicam, gimbal, drone, vehicle rigs"}, {"id": "6f3a2daf-cfef-4899-926d-654f28303ebc", "type": "concept", "title": "Handheld posture and controlled instability"}, {"id": "5fc1fc64-abb2-41eb-aae2-e630fe89ec3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety, rehearsal, marks, and repeatability"}], "description": "The point is to understand movement options and their tradeoffs."}, {"id": "a14a7473-374f-478d-a6f8-121ec7a82f15", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Movement grammar", "children": [{"id": "c9bbb893-f412-4534-a85d-0f4a10399683", "type": "concept", "title": "Axis, screen direction, motivated reframing, and parallax"}, {"id": "65354446-fe3b-47d9-bd9a-33fcb4162316", "type": "concept", "title": "Long takes and blocking complexity"}, {"id": "7d22a642-19c0-46fd-9b92-3ab9a82a9e35", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutting into and out of movement"}], "description": "Students learn how motion affects continuity and audience orientation."}]}, {"id": "74acddd8-3e96-4eac-8b8d-88b8f61a8bd3", "type": "topic", "title": "Light Physics, Fixtures, and Safety", "description": "Before expressive lighting, students need the fundamentals of light behavior, fixture choice, power, and safe set practice.", "children": [{"id": "db1f0266-f6d7-4602-a040-c45207ba3c42", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Light behavior", "children": [{"id": "e77a6d69-c6a9-4aed-8aa6-5ae5c0cb421f", "type": "concept", "title": "Intensity, distance, inverse square law, spread, falloff, and direction"}, {"id": "2f1431ab-51a9-4c1b-8661-8ef3cda462ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Hardness, softness, diffusion, bounce, and negative fill"}, {"id": "47ceba27-e4bf-4a53-9f09-95282486f1c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflection, absorption, transmission, and color temperature"}], "description": "Students learn the physics that makes lighting predictable."}, {"id": "506d47b6-5df6-4a3b-a449-eb2ae35f748b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lighting units and control", "children": [{"id": "96f27cc2-139f-4021-a409-b4b75ed6d19e", "type": "concept", "title": "LED, tungsten, HMI, fluorescent, practicals, tubes, panels, and fresnels"}, {"id": "1ffba21a-1774-4c7d-b853-80de49e41fa4", "type": "concept", "title": "Flags, nets, scrims, grids, cutters, diffusion, and gels"}, {"id": "f3584ce1-e31a-46f8-bb78-20e46bb8d507", "type": "concept", "title": "DMX, dimming, flicker, and fixture limitations"}], "description": "The gist is to know what tools do before placing them."}, {"id": "164b76ae-c66f-4d09-9d54-19f370af06e0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Electrical and set safety", "children": [{"id": "1a785aa8-9a49-44eb-8311-edbf061a7504", "type": "concept", "title": "Load calculations, circuits, batteries, cabling, and weather"}, {"id": "c25bbe85-ed91-470b-aabf-fc397750dad1", "type": "concept", "title": "Grip stands, sandbags, overhead rigging, and hot fixtures"}, {"id": "83daf691-692a-4bbe-a65f-0f78214b02cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Set communication and hazard awareness"}], "description": "Students learn professional habits that prevent injury and equipment failure."}]}, {"id": "e6376ca8-c535-48b5-9f8c-cc37c564ca1a", "type": "topic", "title": "Lighting for Mood, Faces, and Story", "description": "Lighting is where cinematography becomes emotional architecture. This topic trains students to shape faces, spaces, contrast, and atmosphere.", "children": [{"id": "e9292f38-8093-4a25-98d5-73a0a32f5967", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Key, fill, backlight, and contrast", "children": [{"id": "db604560-f3f8-49ff-97b2-8493e1de97a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Three-point lighting and its alternatives"}, {"id": "f99163bb-3f8b-46bc-8e6b-2315d748b7dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting ratios, mood, and genre conventions"}, {"id": "bd908522-ba61-452c-970a-d6dd88b7fea8", "type": "concept", "title": "Silhouette, edge light, toppers, eye light, and wrap"}], "description": "Students learn classic lighting structure as a flexible language."}, {"id": "b2f7f08b-2bdb-4450-9194-c37719f46114", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lighting faces and skin", "children": [{"id": "2f18c65f-059a-4d46-8ee7-567ffb9c5b8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Face shape, skin tone, texture, age, and makeup"}, {"id": "02e8516b-ec66-426f-ba21-458f52c5470e", "type": "concept", "title": "Soft versus hard sources and directionality"}, {"id": "5b4a4b61-b512-4c36-a183-5fb4c7bd5ae0", "type": "concept", "title": "Exposure choices that respect subject dignity"}], "description": "The point is to make ethical and beautiful choices across different people and contexts."}, {"id": "798456e2-df3b-4e14-bda2-e682720a5f3b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Atmosphere and motivated light", "children": [{"id": "512dddec-1d30-4bd8-94a8-525d700c9b16", "type": "concept", "title": "Windows, lamps, screens, signs, fire, moonlight, and streetlight"}, {"id": "65386bab-097b-4500-b4f9-f7e2ca18bf2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Smoke, haze, rain, and texture"}, {"id": "9a7d3a48-098b-4bce-9be1-b216a7366c08", "type": "concept", "title": "Day, night, dawn, dusk, and continuity across time"}], "description": "Students connect light to the world of the scene."}]}, {"id": "d69b6270-c4de-4453-ada7-362200f4e95d", "type": "topic", "title": "Color, Contrast, and Visual Palette", "description": "Color and contrast carry emotion, time, genre, and world-building. This topic links on-set color decisions to post-production and story design.", "children": [{"id": "6b9e2e7e-81f2-4bb0-95ad-9160bc562333", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color theory for cinematography", "children": [{"id": "2aea0606-083c-495b-9f36-d8d5a124125a", "type": "concept", "title": "Complementary, analogous, monochrome, and split palettes"}, {"id": "86ec7932-dee5-4271-9b61-feb882aea857", "type": "concept", "title": "Warm/cool contrast and emotional associations"}, {"id": "93758b3a-7688-469c-9031-ca37e88c0513", "type": "concept", "title": "Color scripts and palette boards"}], "description": "Students learn the visual effects of hue, saturation, value, and temperature."}, {"id": "ae7951f3-71f6-4bfd-b657-46dfb6310544", "type": "subtopic", "title": "White balance and color management", "children": [{"id": "454eed82-655e-4636-9b57-e529d7d072e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Kelvin settings, tint, mixed sources, and gels"}, {"id": "3ee4d52f-a887-4250-8385-da5541337bce", "type": "concept", "title": "Log, LUTs, transforms, ACES concepts, and display-referred images"}, {"id": "58680394-b23b-48ac-aea8-62020346785e", "type": "concept", "title": "Color charts and controlled references"}], "description": "The goal is to maintain control from camera to grade."}, {"id": "e14cb9b5-248f-4b12-80f1-ab2ad4acccbe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contrast and tonal design", "children": [{"id": "2ee7076f-3195-4f06-90c7-539f3f4e52a9", "type": "concept", "title": "High key, low key, noir, naturalism, and stylization"}, {"id": "1acff3a8-c33d-4310-945e-1f857857e105", "type": "concept", "title": "Black levels, highlight rolloff, and skin-tone placement"}, {"id": "f84218bf-72fc-49c4-890d-fac9c5b76321", "type": "concept", "title": "Matching contrast across coverage"}], "description": "Students understand tone as composition."}]}, {"id": "9ea2739a-f67c-4ee6-91bb-ae1e68e0e124", "type": "topic", "title": "Blocking, Coverage, and Director Collaboration", "description": "Great images emerge from performance, staging, and collaboration. This topic teaches students to build shots with directors and actors rather than merely record action.", "children": [{"id": "d50a8442-1adf-4a7f-a0aa-94c71c3327b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Blocking with story intent", "children": [{"id": "0d11c213-6d68-4123-8cb1-d845ac6c45a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Power shifts, entrances, exits, proximity, and reveal"}, {"id": "38b960be-03fb-4f95-b1f5-deaac70e8869", "type": "concept", "title": "Camera position relative to performance"}, {"id": "665e6541-a0b0-4e42-8ae4-475814a688f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Rehearsal as image discovery"}], "description": "Students learn to place camera and actors around dramatic beats."}, {"id": "6b679fff-3d33-49e6-b2a9-0bb6be018387", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Coverage strategy", "children": [{"id": "b0269957-f33b-4b6c-a610-61bf800c45e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Masters, singles, over-the-shoulders, inserts, and cutaways"}, {"id": "6baa29f4-fb6f-42f4-b4af-24a391ff8eaf", "type": "concept", "title": "Shot size progression and emotional escalation"}, {"id": "2e518d27-af33-4581-97ba-abffe44de9bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Efficiency versus expressive specificity"}], "description": "The point is to design shots that edit together and preserve performance."}, {"id": "b9be123c-719d-4c3d-9e3e-581bdd290dd9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Director-DP communication", "children": [{"id": "29544d63-12f4-49e5-b823-92c50b1b6fe6", "type": "concept", "title": "Lookbooks, references, shot lists, overheads, and tests"}, {"id": "191688a5-0ccc-44a9-aa8a-440fb723a8bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Language for mood, lens, movement, and light"}, {"id": "4d92bcbf-094b-45cf-8021-9b5eb5248be1", "type": "concept", "title": "Negotiating creative priorities under constraints"}], "description": "Students practice translating ideas into shootable plans."}]}, {"id": "999baf68-1fae-48f3-b39e-8be20bf36f2c", "type": "topic", "title": "Location, Interior, and Exterior Lighting Practice", "description": "This topic moves students from theory into repeatable setups under real location constraints.", "children": [{"id": "6df7ffe3-e6da-4555-bf2a-323d7e9c6352", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interior lighting setups", "children": [{"id": "0f4b5327-234d-4bfc-bae5-527c9fbe896a", "type": "concept", "title": "Window key, practical augmentation, book lights, negative fill"}, {"id": "73c046a6-902e-40ed-8b07-1c314d749f9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Small room strategy and spill control"}, {"id": "401ca673-5587-4405-925f-5240d02e64ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuity across coverage"}], "description": "Students practice building motivated interiors quickly and safely."}, {"id": "6b6bf8bd-7cd2-46c2-917b-ed20fd3a1acd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exterior lighting setups", "children": [{"id": "4d27e9ab-3f51-48a0-b5d2-7064dad70fe1", "type": "concept", "title": "Sun path, backlight, shade, diffusion, bounce, and negative fill"}, {"id": "d51dc008-2f40-4dab-8f87-26c421628538", "type": "concept", "title": "Golden hour, midday, overcast, and night exterior tactics"}, {"id": "8298d16a-be96-4d63-a7e3-970eadcd78fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Weather, permits, and safety planning"}], "description": "The goal is to work intelligently with the sun and environment."}, {"id": "abd22013-27bb-4083-82de-8f14df5d20a0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Low-light and night work", "children": [{"id": "c7bc86de-e8d0-4a62-99a8-cf115bb55c02", "type": "concept", "title": "Moonlight, streetlight, practicals, and motivated sources"}, {"id": "f52c1609-9eb1-4767-ae24-ae81b480aacf", "type": "concept", "title": "Noise, contrast, color, and exposure strategy"}, {"id": "976d6a1a-da83-4545-a95f-0bd535ea7a8d", "type": "concept", "title": "Power, rigging, crew movement, and visibility"}], "description": "Students learn to design darkness without losing image quality."}]}, {"id": "85d2ed3d-0f4c-4ded-bfa4-fe233f86c828", "type": "topic", "title": "Camera Department, Crew Roles, and Set Protocol", "description": "Cinematography is a team craft. This topic teaches the roles, language, and discipline that keep a set professional.", "children": [{"id": "97db45be-82f9-4faf-9de7-f495dc3ad179", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Camera department roles", "children": [{"id": "15632223-04a3-4478-ad4b-43d13d1e924b", "type": "concept", "title": "DP, camera operator, first AC, second AC, loader/media manager, DIT"}, {"id": "721fd9cc-8585-4b97-b119-4330945e3338", "type": "concept", "title": "Focus, slating, lens changes, builds, and reports"}, {"id": "5db7d2e6-ca6e-4c13-b275-a4b37d7f25aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Respecting chain of command and communication lanes"}], "description": "Students learn who does what and why it matters."}, {"id": "6c83b95f-87ac-4fa8-84a7-dea54fbe6dfc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Grip and electric collaboration", "children": [{"id": "196b8660-d073-425c-940b-092f4f46602b", "type": "concept", "title": "Gaffer, best electric, key grip, dolly grip, swing crew"}, {"id": "dccefb23-3f75-4a88-88e6-a3b353430588", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting plots, rigging, power, stands, flags, and overheads"}, {"id": "8fdfb4b9-ed34-4e56-975d-dbaddbbd41f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Time estimates and safe setup sequencing"}], "description": "The point is to understand how image plans become physical setups."}, {"id": "b90e2bb5-bcff-4df8-b865-aededb190a0c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Set etiquette and leadership", "children": [{"id": "6fb81cfa-ddd8-4ee7-808f-b946d84cd338", "type": "concept", "title": "Clear calls, quiet on set, lockups, and resets"}, {"id": "395d240e-be5d-415c-b1ae-738c145f9721", "type": "concept", "title": "Inclusive, respectful, and harassment-free sets"}, {"id": "d9f9ebfa-1dc7-4351-ad64-8a36f6caee6b", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem escalation and decision ownership"}], "description": "Students practice professional conduct."}]}, {"id": "4fbc7f26-c327-4c7f-9a48-8fb671b4a711", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Cinema Workflow, LUTs, and DIT Practice", "description": "Modern cinematography depends on a reliable image pipeline. This topic teaches students how capture choices flow into dailies, edit, grade, and delivery.", "children": [{"id": "7773119d-0d9a-40b9-b3a7-8cf21b2b9b0a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capture formats", "children": [{"id": "6c0f2fbf-5598-4686-b8eb-6c4b7649b280", "type": "concept", "title": "Raw, ProRes, DNx, H.264/H.265, bit depth, chroma subsampling"}, {"id": "abcb4b75-888c-415c-87d9-27723771b205", "type": "concept", "title": "Resolution, frame rate, data rate, and storage planning"}, {"id": "0fc21fae-945c-4606-af32-e7917ba25567", "type": "concept", "title": "Proxy workflow and editorial handoff"}], "description": "Students understand how codecs and recording settings affect quality and workflow."}, {"id": "44bb50c1-f6b5-4d6b-9eb3-c1f19ceaacb6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Look management", "children": [{"id": "abdc471c-1675-4e50-a3db-1c6de1a8568b", "type": "concept", "title": "Show LUTs, technical LUTs, CDL, and viewing transforms"}, {"id": "9ecfb587-5c0b-4a7e-97f7-9cb80125f340", "type": "concept", "title": "Communicating intended look to post"}, {"id": "4a29326b-ab6d-4078-8b00-1c83b791ae50", "type": "concept", "title": "Dailies, stills, and continuity references"}], "description": "The gist is to separate monitoring looks from recorded image data."}, {"id": "bdccc21e-a57b-412a-a9d7-10161f268a13", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data integrity", "children": [{"id": "b01b5a32-28ba-457a-95d5-5099d1a141dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Card handling, checksum backup, naming, reports, and verification"}, {"id": "536dfab6-831d-4842-8be2-424d46ce7f07", "type": "concept", "title": "DIT station basics and onset color notes"}, {"id": "3f258b26-3a8e-4a32-8073-19f34022a5f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Failure prevention and recovery protocols"}], "description": "Students learn that footage protection is part of cinematography."}]}, {"id": "5da4c0cc-630a-4a48-90ce-cf6cb4fe1f4b", "type": "topic", "title": "Pre-Production, Shot Design, and Visual Planning", "description": "Strong cinematography is designed before the camera rolls. This topic teaches planning documents that turn ideas into images.", "children": [{"id": "d37479a9-a442-4d04-99c3-66df356dc95b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual research and lookbooks", "children": [{"id": "78cdd73e-5e89-49d3-bc70-4cfe37f25731", "type": "concept", "title": "Frames, paintings, photography, texture, color, and genre references"}, {"id": "8f24d45b-ac01-4c73-830f-8094ea738c4a", "type": "concept", "title": "Reference analysis: what to borrow and what to avoid"}, {"id": "b303259b-2bc7-4a9a-a34e-d8054357776a", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual rules and exceptions"}], "description": "Students learn to gather references that guide production rather than merely decorate a pitch."}, {"id": "cf55d7b4-22b9-4771-9cf2-37d3c889f2be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Shot lists and overheads", "children": [{"id": "b17bf650-5c2d-48e2-aa58-f7c788a08102", "type": "concept", "title": "Shot numbering, lenses, movement, size, and coverage notes"}, {"id": "34cfec1a-207d-4939-b4e9-3203b3e60023", "type": "concept", "title": "Floor plans, sun paths, lighting diagrams, and gear lists"}, {"id": "a8a3a8b8-0b39-43f9-a358-114d60600ef5", "type": "concept", "title": "Contingency plans and schedule realism"}], "description": "The point is to translate scenes into efficient production plans."}, {"id": "156f5d4b-af45-4e46-a0c0-cc55da963285", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Camera and lighting tests", "children": [{"id": "cae8fe39-8c03-4432-a966-7f7deb6c160c", "type": "concept", "title": "Lens, filter, LUT, exposure, skin tone, and wardrobe tests"}, {"id": "e2ee9031-7b94-4f86-ba60-b6315b5f425d", "type": "concept", "title": "Location scouts and tech scouts"}, {"id": "e059cf79-9691-413d-90df-5eeb2aa6de8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Test review with director, production design, makeup, and post"}], "description": "Students learn to test assumptions before production."}]}, {"id": "ea03bf95-1cb6-491d-a49f-bae77b399211", "type": "topic", "title": "Genre, Documentary, and Specialized Cinematography", "description": "Different forms ask different things of the camera. This topic prepares students to adapt craft principles across narrative, documentary, commercial, and experimental work.", "children": [{"id": "bde7dce9-80b2-4993-9006-0a7ecc0404d9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Narrative genre language", "children": [{"id": "bc514976-a36e-4694-a487-e8caa87d81fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Comedy, horror, drama, thriller, action, musical, and period work"}, {"id": "0c24badd-0c3e-42ac-a78c-0dc3a9e33e9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Genre conventions and creative deviation"}, {"id": "36d1940a-995d-4df9-a2b3-d76b6d95bb6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual continuity across scenes and acts"}], "description": "Students learn how genre shapes visual expectations."}, {"id": "bbedfd49-f48a-45e5-ad1f-099a8a1ef357", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Documentary cinematography", "children": [{"id": "b8512a79-6a27-47b9-bd50-90b8498e9b5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Interviews, verite, b-roll, observational shooting, and access"}, {"id": "20262baf-a9f1-4f7b-8340-239207a2c107", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, vulnerability, and representational responsibility"}, {"id": "157c63bf-f095-453e-90d3-0a7f4acdb128", "type": "concept", "title": "Small-crew mobility and available-light strategy"}], "description": "The goal is to balance responsiveness, ethics, and image quality."}, {"id": "0a123efc-146e-4fe1-ab6b-cf36bfda03e5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Specialized techniques", "children": [{"id": "d2fdde5d-c29d-43b8-8626-e251b555378a", "type": "concept", "title": "Green screen, VFX plates, high speed, time-lapse, macro, underwater, drone"}, {"id": "2bcd046a-a951-4b7f-b731-92399d1c360e", "type": "concept", "title": "Product, music video, and branded-content lighting"}, {"id": "904c3a3f-a1f3-4043-8002-0e49e3423808", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety, permits, insurance, and specialist crew"}], "description": "Students survey techniques that require extra planning."}]}, {"id": "9f94a362-bc66-4b67-8606-d93432e82ac6", "type": "topic", "title": "Critique, Visual Analysis, and Professional Taste", "description": "Students grow by learning to see precisely and speak about images usefully. This topic builds critique habits that improve both craft and collaboration.", "children": [{"id": "cdae7c86-2431-4564-9182-72d3be432843", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Shot analysis", "children": [{"id": "7f75208d-9fc7-465a-956f-7fea3ea3cddd", "type": "concept", "title": "Lens, composition, exposure, color, light, movement, and blocking"}, {"id": "50a7f5ec-2902-4951-98f9-0dff1afbfe30", "type": "concept", "title": "Cause-and-effect analysis rather than taste alone"}, {"id": "4e0d7ed7-2dee-4f56-877f-9e373308dfc2", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparing student work with professional references"}], "description": "Students practice diagnosing how an image works."}, {"id": "34872a27-3abe-4664-8a59-01829321c759", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critique language", "children": [{"id": "88da1a52-0de7-40f2-b1c8-7649e7df9f71", "type": "concept", "title": "Intention, execution, audience effect, and revision paths"}, {"id": "7f425f7e-d5d4-4ee9-bc76-1dae87627b10", "type": "concept", "title": "Separating technical issues from creative choices"}, {"id": "bb3b8cae-4b31-4669-8ed6-785c12a85e28", "type": "concept", "title": "Receiving critique without defensiveness"}], "description": "The point is to give feedback that is specific, respectful, and actionable."}, {"id": "c7ee3b2a-aa2b-442e-8129-8e56bf67c0ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Developing taste", "children": [{"id": "9b42304b-316e-4e8d-954d-9a125af93fc8", "type": "concept", "title": "Shot journals and frame studies"}, {"id": "4734e147-a410-42d3-9dfe-94a5b756c8e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Cinematographer research and ASC-style interviews"}, {"id": "c8c35e41-139b-4465-8c0d-6184c719679e", "type": "concept", "title": "Personal visual grammar and growth goals"}], "description": "Students learn that taste is trained through viewing and making."}]}, {"id": "6fcdf237-2285-4121-a858-3db3e64faa43", "type": "topic", "title": "Ethics, Representation, and Sustainable Production", "description": "Images have social consequences. This topic teaches students to make responsible visual choices about people, labor, environment, and power.", "children": [{"id": "91df2506-a23c-4755-801d-598f7c553c05", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Representation and gaze", "children": [{"id": "756f0026-984c-4df6-87d8-366909f24f96", "type": "concept", "title": "Framing bodies, communities, violence, poverty, and intimacy"}, {"id": "39b599e4-b120-4a89-90b2-65989a0de605", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, vulnerability, and image ownership"}, {"id": "2c68a27a-f8d1-45f7-ad90-7aa1c894f362", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural consultation and context"}], "description": "Students examine how camera choices can dignify, stereotype, objectify, or empower."}, {"id": "af261dbf-6676-415b-b085-90d6c2822b5f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Set ethics", "children": [{"id": "961ea350-a660-4e05-8b0f-7a602f670a11", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety, rest, communication, harassment prevention, and accessibility"}, {"id": "f0294129-cbb7-4088-8f9f-bbf052a38ecd", "type": "concept", "title": "Working with actors, minors, stunts, intimacy, and sensitive material"}, {"id": "a592d2a0-ce0a-43ec-adb8-7bc0dc4c16d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Leadership under pressure"}], "description": "The goal is to connect image ambition to humane labor practice."}, {"id": "8b70d107-8022-4ad7-91ad-56fbb937a2e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sustainable production", "children": [{"id": "adeeebba-2d3d-418b-aa52-9ff69e0db3dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Power use, batteries, generators, transport, and waste"}, {"id": "04378b54-d954-4680-9925-5e5040736c45", "type": "concept", "title": "LED efficiency and location impact"}, {"id": "9388254c-e6b4-490b-9d68-8048a9bb6fc3", "type": "concept", "title": "Planning choices that reduce unnecessary footprint"}], "description": "Students learn basic ecological responsibility in camera and lighting practice."}]}, {"id": "650ee35e-27dd-4dd0-9c80-060072e1cb54", "type": "topic", "title": "Cinematography Portfolio and Final Scene Project", "description": "The capstone converts practice into evidence of growth. Students create a scene or visual sequence and curate a portfolio that shows intention, craft, and reflection.", "children": [{"id": "11e50d25-cfd5-464a-92c3-c14e4e31d20a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Final scene project", "children": [{"id": "c91e9ddb-cdca-4184-8aef-3f9cce86c4c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Script breakdown, references, lookbook, and shot list"}, {"id": "f9c11506-73ce-43a4-9c27-3f791900ddd6", "type": "concept", "title": "Production, lighting plan, camera reports, and footage management"}, {"id": "e297c0be-d462-48ed-bf01-a18b412b749d", "type": "concept", "title": "Rough cut, grade notes, and final delivery"}], "description": "Students synthesize camera, light, movement, color, and collaboration in a complete short sequence."}, {"id": "c5c8469c-eab3-494c-8609-7a100524e6e5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio curation", "children": [{"id": "3bc6e539-cc2b-468c-8195-750303088942", "type": "concept", "title": "Selected frames, lighting diagrams, before/after stills, and final clips"}, {"id": "99a57e73-78cf-47a2-8834-8f8c296be0b0", "type": "concept", "title": "DP statement and project context"}, {"id": "09621828-fb44-4592-9a1a-4771ec08ba58", "type": "concept", "title": "Reel structure, credits, and permissions"}], "description": "The point is to present work professionally."}, {"id": "49cdd965-a72e-4bc7-b487-ed7470ebf99b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reflection and next steps", "children": [{"id": "431f3785-169d-4382-8f5e-56e9b2e5ccfc", "type": "concept", "title": "Technical strengths and weaknesses"}, {"id": "c035d583-d3f7-459b-8f39-0d958edf868c", "type": "concept", "title": "Collaboration lessons and production constraints"}, {"id": "84ab7abe-7c56-4d3c-8162-62d2cee629a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Personal cinematography goals and practice plan"}], "description": "Students learn to evaluate their own process and plan future growth."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$cinejson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
  'course',
  'public'
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.learning_paths where slug = 'cinematography'
