tch."}, {"id": "cf55d7b4-22b9-4771-9cf2-37d3c889f2be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Shot lists and overheads", "children": [{"id": "b17bf650-5c2d-48e2-aa58-f7c788a08102", "type": "concept", "title": "Shot numbering, lenses, movement, size, and coverage notes"}, {"id": "34cfec1a-207d-4939-b4e9-3203b3e60023", "type": "concept", "title": "Floor plans, sun paths, lighting diagrams, and gear lists"}, {"id": "a8a3a8b8-0b39-43f9-a358-114d60600ef5", "type": "concept", "title": "Contingency plans and schedule realism"}], "description": "The point is to translate scenes into efficient production plans."}, {"id": "156f5d4b-af45-4e46-a0c0-cc55da963285", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Camera and lighting tests", "children": [{"id": "cae8fe39-8c03-4432-a966-7f7deb6c160c", "type": "concept", "title": "Lens, filter, LUT, exposure, skin tone, and wardrobe tests"}, {"id": "e2ee9031-7b94-4f86-ba60-b6315b5f425d", "type": "concept", "title": "Location scouts and tech scouts"}, {"id": "e059cf79-9691-413d-90df-5eeb2aa6de8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Test review with director, production design, makeup, and post"}], "description": "Students learn to test assumptions before production."}]}, {"id": "ea03bf95-1cb6-491d-a49f-bae77b399211", "type": "topic", "title": "Genre, Documentary, and Specialized Cinematography", "description": "Different forms ask different things of the camera. This topic prepares students to adapt craft principles across narrative, documentary, commercial, and experimental work.", "children": [{"id": "bde7dce9-80b2-4993-9006-0a7ecc0404d9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Narrative genre language", "children": [{"id": "bc514976-a36e-4694-a487-e8caa87d81fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Comedy, horror, drama, thriller, action, musical, and period work"}, {"id": "0c24badd-0c3e-42ac-a78c-0dc3a9e33e9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Genre conventions and creative deviation"}, {"id": "36d1940a-995d-4df9-a2b3-d76b6d95bb6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual continuity across scenes and acts"}], "description": "Students learn how genre shapes visual expectations."}, {"id": "bbedfd49-f48a-45e5-ad1f-099a8a1ef357", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Documentary cinematography", "children": [{"id": "b8512a79-6a27-47b9-bd50-90b8498e9b5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Interviews, verite, b-roll, observational shooting, and access"}, {"id": "20262baf-a9f1-4f7b-8340-239207a2c107", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, vulnerability, and representational responsibility"}, {"id": "157c63bf-f095-453e-90d3-0a7f4acdb128", "type": "concept", "title": "Small-crew mobility and available-light strategy"}], "description": "The goal is to balance responsiveness, ethics, and image quality."}, {"id": "0a123efc-146e-4fe1-ab6b-cf36bfda03e5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Specialized techniques", "children": [{"id": "d2fdde5d-c29d-43b8-8626-e251b555378a", "type": "concept", "title": "Green screen, VFX plates, high speed, time-lapse, macro, underwater, drone"}, {"id": "2bcd046a-a951-4b7f-b731-92399d1c360e", "type": "concept", "title": "Product, music video, and branded-content lighting"}, {"id": "904c3a3f-a1f3-4043-8002-0e49e3423808", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety, permits, insurance, and specialist crew"}], "description": "Students survey techniques that require extra planning."}]}, {"id": "9f94a362-bc66-4b67-8606-d93432e82ac6", "type": "topic", "title": "Critique, Visual Analysis, and Professional Taste", "description": "Students grow by learning to see precisely and speak about images usefully. This topic builds critique habits that improve both craft and collaboration.", "children": [{"id": "cdae7c86-2431-4564-9182-72d3be432843", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Shot analysis", "children": [{"id": "7f75208d-9fc7-465a-956f-7fea3ea3cddd", "type": "concept", "title": "Lens, composition, exposure, color, light, movement, and blocking"}, {"id": "50a7f5ec-2902-4951-98f9-0dff1afbfe30", "type": "concept", "title": "Cause-and-effect analysis rather than taste alone"}, {"id": "4e0d7ed7-2dee-4f56-877f-9e373308dfc2", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparing student work with professional references"}], "description": "Students practice diagnosing how an image works."}, {"id": "34872a27-3abe-4664-8a59-01829321c759", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critique language", "children": [{"id": "88da1a52-0de7-40f2-b1c8-7649e7df9f71", "type": "concept", "title": "Intention, execution, audience effect, and revision paths"}, {"id": "7f425f7e-d5d4-4ee9-bc76-1dae87627b10", "type": "concept", "title": "Separating technical issues from creative choices"}, {"id": "bb3b8cae-4b31-4669-8ed6-785c12a85e28", "type": "concept", "title": "Receiving critique without defensiveness"}], "description": "The point is to give feedback that is specific, respectful, and actionable."}, {"id": "c7ee3b2a-aa2b-442e-8129-8e56bf67c0ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Developing taste", "children": [{"id": "9b42304b-316e-4e8d-954d-9a125af93fc8", "type": "concept", "title": "Shot journals and frame studies"}, {"id": "4734e147-a410-42d3-9dfe-94a5b756c8e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Cinematographer research and ASC-style interviews"}, {"id": "c8c35e41-139b-4465-8c0d-6184c719679e", "type": "concept", "title": "Personal visual grammar and growth goals"}], "description": "Students learn that taste is trained through viewing and making."}]}, {"id": "6fcdf237-2285-4121-a858-3db3e64faa43", "type": "topic", "title": "Ethics, Representation, and Sustainable Production", "description": "Images have social consequences. This topic teaches students to make responsible visual choices about people, labor, environment, and power.", "children": [{"id": "91df2506-a23c-4755-801d-598f7c553c05", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Representation and gaze", "children": [{"id": "756f0026-984c-4df6-87d8-366909f24f96", "type": "concept", "title": "Framing bodies, communities, violence, poverty, and intimacy"}, {"id": "39b599e4-b120-4a89-90b2-65989a0de605", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, vulnerabi